When creating a git commit, use a multi-line message (HEREDOC), never a single paragraph.

Format:
- Line 1: short subject, imperative, max ~72 characters
- Blank line
- Body grouped under subheadings with bullet points
- Group by area (Header, Footer, Data, Tasks, etc.)
- Each bullet is one concrete change; do not restated the whole diff
- Skip empty headings

Example:

Add footer, contact links, and brand icons

Footer
- Add the Footer component with navigation and contact blocks
- Include brand icons for the contact row

Data
- Link the address in contact data for accessibility

Tasks
- Mark the footer item complete in TASKS.md